%U A397470 3424261526610033195216736412566,363723145401966899965138490916962925,83697427029624980036553534713693244053626
%N A397470 Number of strongly connected digraphs on n labeled nodes that are reducible as a flow graph with entry node 1.
%C A397470 The 'loop regions' of reducible flow graphs: every reducible flow graph decomposes uniquely into such regions (its SCCs) joined by an acyclic header-entering superstructure.
%C A397470 a(n) = Sum over single-source reducible cores D on n nodes rooted at node 1 of Product_{sink SCCs s of D}(2^|s|-1) * 2^(n-1-Sum|s|): the back-edge sets into the root that make D strongly connected.
%D A397470 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A397470 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A397470 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A397470 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%F A397470 a(n) = Sum_D 2^(n-1-s(D)) * Product_{C in sinkSCC(D)} (2^|C|-1), where D ranges over single-source reducible digraphs on n labeled nodes rooted at node 1 and s(D) is the total number of vertices in the sink SCCs of D.
%o A397470 (Python) reducible_labeled_system(14)[2] # See Python link in A398465 for program code.
%Y A397470 Cf. A398465, A003030 (all strongly connected digraphs, unrooted).
%K A397470 nonn
%O A397470 1,3
%A A397470 _Gregory Morse_, Aug 05 2026
